  ('BIO 154', 'General Biology Practicals', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '100 Level', 'second', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('PHY 112', 'General Physics for Life Science II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Concepts of heat, temperature: measurement of temperature, clinical thermometer. Heat capacity, specific heat, latent heat, calorimetry. Gas laws; kinetic theory of gases. Thermal energy, isothermal and adiabatic changes. Conduction, convection; radiation. Sound waves; intensity, pitch and quality of sound. Propagation of sound in solids, liquids and gases. Doppler effect. The ear. Reflection and refraction of light; plane and spherical mirrors, thin lenses; optical instruments. The eye, defects of vision and their corrections. Wave nature of light, interference, diffraction: velocity of light.', '["Concepts of heat and temperature: measurement, clinical thermometer, heat capacity, calorimetry", "Gas laws; kinetic theory of gases; thermal energy, isothermal and adiabatic changes", "Conduction, convection and radiation", "Sound waves: intensity, pitch, quality; propagation in solids, liquids and gases; Doppler effect; the ear", "Reflection and refraction of light: mirrors, thin lenses, optical instruments", "The eye, defects of vision and their corrections", "Wave nature of light: interference, diffraction, velocity of light"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('PHY 114', 'General Physics for Life Science III', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Electric charge, Coulomb''s Law, electric field, electrostatic potential. Energy in electric field, capacitors. Dielectrics. Electric current, potential difference and electromotive force. Ohm''s Law: potentiometer, metre bridge, Wheatstone bridge. Magnetic effects of currents; permanent magnetism, earth''s magnetic field. Faraday''s Law of induction, generators and electric motor. Alternating currents; Maxwell''s equations. Structure of the atom. Radioactivity, X-rays, applications in life sciences. Nuclear energy.', '["Electric charge, Coulomb''s Law, electric field, electrostatic potential", "Energy in electric field, capacitors; dielectrics", "Electric current, potential difference and electromotive force; Ohm''s Law", "Magnetic effects of currents; permanent magnetism, earth''s magnetic field", "Faraday''s Law of induction, generators and electric motor; alternating currents; Maxwell''s equations", "Structure of the atom; radioactivity, X-rays, applications in life sciences; nuclear energy"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('CHM 112', 'Basic Principles of Physical Chemistry II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Gas laws and kinetic theory: kinetic theory of gases, elementary derivation and deduction of gas laws, molecular speeds, deviations from ideal behaviour, van der Waals modification, and gas liquefaction. Phase equilibrium and solutions: phase transitions and phase equilibria in one-component systems; ideal solutions, Raoult''s law, Henry''s law, real solutions, and colligative properties. Thermodynamics and kinetics: aspects of the first law of thermodynamics, thermochemistry, entropy, free energy, and spontaneous changes; ionic equilibria, acids, bases, indicators, and buffers; elementary chemical kinetics.', '["Gas laws and kinetic theory of gases; molecular speeds; deviations from ideal behaviour; gas liquefaction", "Phase transitions and phase equilibria; ideal and real solutions; colligative properties", "First law of thermodynamics, thermochemistry, entropy, free energy, spontaneous changes", "Ionic equilibria, acids, bases, indicators and buffers", "Elementary chemical kinetics: rate laws, order and molecularity, Arrhenius equation"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('CHM 122', 'Basic Principles of Organic Chemistry III', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Structure and classification: historical survey of organic chemistry, IUPAC nomenclature, classification of organic compounds, homologous series, elemental analysis, molecular formulas, and structural isomerism. Bonding and reactivity: isolation and purification methods, functional group concepts, resonance, and aromaticity. Functional groups: saturated and unsaturated hydrocarbons, cyclic hydrocarbons, alcohols, alkyl halides, ethers, aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids, amines, and aromatic compounds. Stereochemistry and lipids: introduction to oils, fats, and stereoisomerism.', '["Historical survey of organic chemistry, IUPAC nomenclature, classification of organic compounds, structural isomerism", "Isolation and purification methods; functional group concepts; resonance and aromaticity", "Saturated and unsaturated hydrocarbons, alcohols, alkyl halides, ethers, aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids, amines, aromatic compounds", "Introduction to oils, fats, and stereoisomerism"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('GSP 102', 'The Use of English II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Part A: Basic Grammar: Introduction. The concept of grammar and its place in language teaching and learning. Parts of speech and their functions (treated in detail). Closed and open class items in parts of speech, Nominalization, Grammatical Structures: the phrase, the clause and the sentence. Elementary Clause Analysis, Sentence Types, Elements and Patterns. Agreement (Grammatical agreement, Notional agreement, Proximity agreement) Agreement with the correlatives. Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology identification and correction.

Part B: Varieties of writing. Introduction (The Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, Writing Types or Genres and their Characteristics). The paragraph as the basic unit of an essay (Types, Development of the Paragraph, Methods of Paragraph Development, The thesis statement). Point of view and style in writing. Qualities of a good piece of writing: Form, Diction and Content in writing. The Mechanics of Writing: punctuation, spelling and capitalization.

Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme. Deciding your genre. Choosing and developing your plot. Point of view, setting and characterization. Using the language that works. Essay Writing — Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation. Technical Writing: Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes, own story for practice, Computer-linked writing, types, style, language, and process.', '["Part A: Basic Grammar - The concept of grammar, Parts of speech, Grammatical Structures, Sentence Types, Agreement, Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology", "Part B: Varieties of writing - Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, the paragraph as the basic unit of an essay, the thesis statement, Qualities of a good piece of writing, Mechanics of Writing", "Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme, plot, point of view, setting and characterization", "Essay Writing - Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation", "Technical Writing - Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('CHM 201', 'General Inorganic Chemistry', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Periodic trends: ionization potential, electron affinity, and electronegativity. Chemical bonding: electrostatic and non-electrostatic valence forces, non-valence cohesive forces. Coordination compounds: introduction to complexes, focusing on colour, magnetic properties, and practical applications.

Prerequisite: CHM 101, or a pass in Chemistry at H.S.C./G.C.E. A-Level', '["Periodic trends: ionization potential, electron affinity, and electronegativity", "Chemical bonding: electrostatic and non-electrostatic valence forces, non-valence cohesive forces", "Coordination compounds: complexes, colour, magnetic properties and practical applications"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('CHM 211', 'General Physical Chemistry', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Gases and thermodynamics: molecular collisions in gases, virial equation, critical phenomena, and reduced properties; chemical thermodynamics, detailed treatment of the first law of thermodynamics, and the Carnot cycle. Chemical kinetics: integrated rate equations for second and third order reactions, reaction mechanisms, rate laws, and the effect of temperature on reaction rates.

Prerequisite: CHM 112', '["Molecular collisions in gases, virial equation, critical phenomena, reduced properties", "Chemical thermodynamics: first law of thermodynamics; the Carnot cycle", "Integrated rate equations for second and third order reactions; reaction mechanisms and rate laws", "Effect of temperature on reaction rates"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('CHM 221', 'General Organic Chemistry I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('CHM 273', 'Practical Organic Chemistry I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('COS 101', 'Introduction to Computer Science', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Concepts of hardware and software; basic subsystems of a digital computer; characteristics of a digital computer; devices/media; types/classes of computer emphasising the PC; history of computers and their generations. Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program. Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming. Booting and shutdown; types of operating system; user interface; managing information, computer malware (virus, etc); computer network; internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc. Office applications; use of a statistical package and a database management system.', '["Concepts of hardware and software","basic subsystems of a digital computer","characteristics of a digital computer","devices/media","types/classes of computer emphasising the PC","history of computers and their generations","Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program","Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming","Booting and shutdown","types of operating system","user interface","managing information, computer malware (virus, etc)","computer network","internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc","Office applications","use of a statistical package and a database management system"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Computer Science course outline'),
  ('MCB 201', 'General Microbiology I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 3, 'General review of the nature and biology of protozoa, fungi, algae, bacteria, archaea and viruses. General characteristics, growth and reproduction of microorganisms. Microbiology methods and instrumentation. Sterilisation and disinfection. Microorganisms in various environments: soil, water, food, etc. Industrial use of microorganisms. Pathogenic role of microorganisms.

Pre-requisite: MCB 102', '["Nature and biology of protozoa, fungi, algae, bacteria, archaea and viruses", "General characteristics, growth and reproduction of microorganisms", "Microbiology methods and instrumentation", "Sterilisation and disinfection", "Microorganisms in various environments: soil, water, food", "Industrial use of microorganisms", "Pathogenic role of microorganisms"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('STA 203', 'Statistics for Agricultural and Biology Science I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Biochemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Initial steps in planning of biological experiments. Methods of data collection, presentation and analysis. Measures of central tendency and dispersion. Frequency distributions. Elementary probability. Discrete and continuous distributions: Binomial, Poisson, Normal and exponential distributions. Interval estimation.', '["Initial steps in planning of biological experiments", "Methods of data collection, presentation and analysis", "Measures of central tendency and dispersion", "Frequency distributions", "Elementary probability", "Discrete and continuous distributions: Binomial, Poisson, Normal and exponential distributions", "Interval estimation"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics handbook'),
